I’ll inspect the measurement metadata and diffraction profile first, then identify candidate phases and carry the best structural models through a GSAS-II refinement. I’ll keep the phase count evidence-driven and report any ambiguity rather than forcing a complete assignment.

The chemistry points first to cobalt tungstate, but I’m treating CoO, WO₃, cobalt oxides, and alternate cobalt–tungsten oxides as live candidates. I’m now extracting the observed peak set and matching it against the local crystallographic database before deciding how many phases the refinement actually supports.

The first full-pattern model confirms two phases: monoclinic WO₃ plus CoWO₄ reaches \(R_{wp}\approx 7.41\%\), and the refined cells land close to known values. I’m comparing the closely related triclinic WO₃ model now; this distinction matters because their strongest peaks nearly coincide, so it has to be decided from the weaker splittings and the whole-profile residual.

The lower-symmetry WO₃ model is favored, but I’m also checking it against a second, independently reported monoclinic structure so that the choice is not an artifact of one old coordinate set. In parallel, I’m replacing the unstable unconstrained profile coefficients with phase-size/strain broadening; that gives a more defensible physical profile and tests how sensitive the ~68:32 phase ratio is to line-shape assumptions.

The phase-count check is now settled: adding fixed, chemically plausible CoO or Co₃O₄ does not improve the converged fit (Co₃O₄ refines to zero; CoO is unstable and worsens \(R_{wp}\)). Refining only the symmetry-allowed Co and W positions in CoWO₄ gives physically sensible coordinates and a reproducible two-phase fit over the entire measured range, with approximately 69.2 wt% WO₃ and 30.8 wt% CoWO₄.

All required deliverables are now written from the same converged GSAS-II project. I’m doing a final consistency pass: re-opening the GPX, re-importing both CIFs, checking that the fractions sum to one, and confirming every row of `fit.csv` satisfies observed − calculated = difference.

Completed the two-phase refinement:

- Triclinic WO₃ (`P -1`): 69.24 wt%
- CoWO₄ (`P 2/c`): 30.76 wt%
- Fit: \(R_{wp}=6.10\%\), \(R_p=4.67\%\), GOF = 1.86

Fractions are normalized over modeled crystalline phases; practical uncertainty is approximately ±2 wt%.

